2:T724,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does IKEA kitchen fitting cost in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, fitting labour may typically cost around £2,000 to £5,000, excluding the kitchen. Complex layouts or additional renovation work can take the total above this range. Every project differs, so obtain a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does IKEA kitchen installation include plumbing and electrics?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not always. Some fitting quotes cover cabinets only, while plumbing, electrical work, appliance connections and lighting are priced separately. Check the written quotation carefully."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to fit an IKEA kitchen yourself?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"DIY fitting may reduce labour costs, but some parts of the project may still require professional tradespeople, such as electrical, gas or specialist plumbing work. Consider the tools, time and experience needed before deciding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is usually not included in an IKEA kitchen fitting quote?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Common exclusions can include kitchen units, appliances, worktops, old-kitchen disposal, flooring, tiling, decorating, service alterations and specialist worktop fabrication. Always request an itemised quote."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I reduce the cost of fitting an IKEA kitchen?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping the existing layout and service positions may reduce labour. You can also compare itemised quotes, choose a suitable worktop and decide in advance which preparation or finishing tasks you will complete yourself."}}]}7:["slug","how-much-does-ikea-kitchen-fitting-cost","d"]
